orking tree, and re-ran the five checks here. All five pass: `tests/test_api.py` (212 passed), ruff, `gen:types`, `tsc -b` and lint. Nothing in `src/` or `web/src/` mentions `mtgo_read_at_startup` any more.\n\n- **API:** the `LiveStatus` field, its default (`False`) and description follow the spec. The docstring now says `watching` and `mtgo_watching` are both asked of the watcher object directly, and `live()` passes the new field.\n- **Texts:** the Live panel now reads \"MTGO is watched too: each game appears once it ends.\" The Settings hint for a set folder reads \"Each game is read once it ends.\"\n- **Types:** `web/src/types/api.ts` was regenerated, not hand-edited.\n\n`docs/status.md` still mentions the old behavior and name. Docs were out of scope, so I left it.\n\nI only ran the commands the spec lists, not the full pytest suite or the frontend tests and build.", "ttft_ms": 1787, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 158753, "uuid": "d8396130-7ca8-41c0-9942-54974e2a96e0", "ttft_stream_ms": 1386, "time_to_request_ms": 54, "first_content_frame_ms": 1386, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
